1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
[Recorded run F03 · 27 Oct 2026 · not live]
Teams now let coding agents propose changes.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,000
This run was recorded on 27 October.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Asked to raise payment retries to 10,
Meta's model, as Proposer,

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,500
claimed that 10 attempts comply
with any documented limit.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,500
[Demo project · 7 seeded memory records]
The demo project's memory says the opposite:

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,500
retries are capped at 3.

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
A single agent would have shipped that claim.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,500
Hyphae Consensus gives that change three roles,
all Meta's model:

9
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,500
a Proposer, a Critic
and an Evidence Evaluator.

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:36,500
The runtime, not a model,
fetches the records and checks their proofs.

11
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:40,000
A fixed policy recommends.
Only a person decides.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
[Recorded run F03 · not live]
Here is how the Meta API is used.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,500
This run made six calls, each recorded
with Meta's request id,

14
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,500
its latency and its token counts:
6,874 in, 31,910 out.

15
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,000
Every call sends a strict JSON schema for its role.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,500
Under protocol 1.3 the Evaluator's schema
is built per call,

17
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:03,500
one required key per claim
and per open objection,

18
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,500
so nothing can be skipped in silence.
And it fails closed.

19
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,000
[Recorded run M04 · 30 Oct 2026 · not live]
In run M04, on 30 October,
the Evaluator left a contradiction unjudged:

20
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
the runtime refused the answer
and issued no recommendation.

21
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[Guided example · scripted roles · SIMULATED evidence · no model call]
To watch the steps, a guided example:

22
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
scripted roles, simulated evidence,
no model called.

23
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,500
The Proposer claims, the Critic objects,
the Evaluator judges each claim,

24
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:30,000
the Proposer revises,
and the round runs again.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,500
[Recorded run F03 · not live]
In F03 the revision went back to 3 attempts
with 50 millisecond jitter,

26
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,500
and all 5 claims were corroborated.

27
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:41,000
Still contested: 6 objections stay open,

28
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
three missing tests, two unsupported claims
and one duplicate-charge risk.

29
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,500
Each claim is tied to the records
that back it or contradict it.

30
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:54,000
Every record came with a Hyphae recall proof,
verified at run time against a pinned anchor:

31
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
all six valid in the final round.

32
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,500
Valid means this is the record that was stored.

33
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,000
It does not mean the record is true.

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,500
The proof files stay with the operator;

35
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:10,000
anyone can re-check the chain.

36
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,500
Every record is hash-chained.

37
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:17,000
This browser just downloaded the archived log
and recomputed every hash:

38
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,500
all 189 records check out,

39
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:23,500
and the file matches the digest
pinned in the archive's manifest.

40
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:27,000
The log is unsigned, so this shows
nothing changed since pinning,

41
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
not that anything in it is true.

42
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[Guided example · SIMULATED evidence]
The run stops at a decision point.

43
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Only a person approves or rejects,

44
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
and on this public portal
the decision carries no authority:

45
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
approving records a choice
and executes nothing.

46
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
This is the guided run;
a recorded run is read-only.

47
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,500
Hyphae Consensus: agent recommendations
you can inspect, check and hold to account

48
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:57,000
before anyone acts.

49
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Its three roles run on Meta's muse-wonder-1.0;
we built it with Muse Code.
